# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# TWO RULES, 2026-08-20, and the number is the point.
#
# Until today this file carried forty. Thirty-eight of them pointed old page URLs at whichever
# door had absorbed their content -- /proof, /world, /company, /customers, /now, /glossary,
# /director, /shadow, /method, /simplified, /project, /tours, /wip-flow, /platform,
# /method-casebook, /supplier, /sim. Behind them sat a whole apparatus: a RETIRED state in the
# IA register, a `retired_areas()` reader, a control asserting no published link pointed at a
# redirect source, a redirect-source exclusion in two separate reachability walkers, and a
# fold register mapping each retired page to the door it folded into.
#
# The director's ruling: "no one has ever visited those URLs. There is no history to protect,
# so stop protecting it." He is right, and the cost was not the four lines of config -- it was
# the machinery, which broke three controls this week and made "delete a page" a day's work.
#
# WHAT SURVIVES, and why each is a real reader's path rather than a preserved history:
#
#   /favicon.ico  -- browsers request this URL on their own, unprompted, whatever the site
#                    links. Without the rule every page load takes a 404 on it. Nobody typed
#                    it and nobody bookmarked it; the browser asks regardless.
#
# AND ONE THAT WENT THE SAME DAY IT WAS KEPT. I kept a `www.poesys.net/* -> poesys.net/:splat`
# rule on the reasoning that "people type www". Then I checked, and www.poesys.net HAS NO DNS
# RECORD -- `getent hosts www.poesys.net` returns nothing, curl cannot connect. A request to
# www never reaches Cloudflare Pages at all, so the rule could not fire for anyone, ever. I had
# kept it on a belief while deleting thirty-eight rules for being kept on a belief.
#
# If www is ever pointed at this site, it is one line, added back with a reason that has been
# checked rather than assumed.
#
# Anything added here in future should have to answer the same question: whose journey breaks
# without it, today?
/favicon.ico /favicon.svg 301
